#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:5
#: 3c2f78337e8546fba51bb390f5d7b5c5
msgid "Archived: DJI F330 FlameWheel QuadCopter Assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:7
#: ca11607c38514f51938e70429a25f942
msgid "This article provides and overview of the DJI F330 FlameWheel QuadCopter, and instructions for how it may be assembled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:11
#: 62b5338a919b42238aeca266ec6a7658
msgid "The DJI F330 FlameWheel is inexpensive, sturdy and small."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:13
#: f50da2cacea94701b8df5f94411b46a0
msgid "It can be flown indoors or out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:14
#: 6a2007f993cd46939e991e2488bec303
msgid "Even though it is compact, the F330 is substantial and can easily carry a battery that will permit 15 minute flights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:16
#: f4fb72dde30543668707e7e84c816b46
msgid "The F330 can carry a GoPro type camera or FPV system if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:17
#: f07c9757e31e4c89a09ec080c311e460
msgid "The ARF (Almost Ready to Fly) kit is a super bargain and includes motors, ESCs (Electronic Speed Controls) and Propellers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:19
#: a2b6d9ca723e48e9992184af90e88e24
msgid "The DJI Motors and ESCs provided in the ARF kit are of high quality, very durable and long lasting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:21
#: e868b8c14c424f73a2f272a8975a056b
msgid "The frame is extremely rugged and all replacement parts are readily available and inexpensive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:25
#: ada052514f0146fa8470c4907776ccd4
msgid "The DJI F450 Flamewheel is an excellent larger alternative to the F330"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:27
#: 698da0b2bdac43acbafc00b52339bd5d
msgid "The F450 FlameWheel ARF kit has a larger frame, 30 amp ESCs and 10\" props for only $10.00 more than the F330."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:29
#: 81edef17512e4b19a9691f1f8f5c27f5
msgid "The F450 is well suited to carrying a GoPro camera, brushless gimbal, landing gear and a larger battery for longer flights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:31
#: 242dfbf2f5da48b5ab343fafa73f04c1
msgid "The F330 and F450 FlameWheel are excellent platforms for the PX4 and PixHawk autopilots as well as the APM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:34
#: 12480ac89d15489894f8c57238441359
msgid "I  have, in fact, converted my personal F330 to use the PX4 autopilot with great success."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:36
#: 9997d228a2054ce1aa9a87770abd516d
msgid "I strongly recommend the F330 and F450 ARF kits, they are reliable, rugged and inexpensive and are suitable for many uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:39
#: 369f6aecedd1414e9ddf5d0f61d8dd5d
msgid "The quality is excellent, the components provide long trouble free service, and replacement parts are cheap and available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:41
#: e39625d5b15a49328070bc49204aea95
msgid "I genuinely don't think you can find a better deal in an APM / PX4 / Pixhawk compatible MultiCopter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:45
#: b74f6c6d44274612b1047ff46db7816c
msgid "Components required in addition to the Flamewheel ARF kit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:47
#: 6f2e7177df4e43e68d333bca5e41511f
msgid "An autopilot (APM 2.6, PX4FMU + PX4IO or Pixhawk) with UBlox GPS module and power supply module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:49
#: 9fd981c7bc97409e968458c438ca3bb1
msgid "RC equipment: RC transmitter and a 5+ channel radio receiver (PPM-SUM compatible for PX4 or Pixhawk)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:51
#: de27522b3d334a8aa1323031d7c90574
msgid "A 3 cell 1800mah to 2650mah LiPo battery and an appropriate battery Charger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:53
#: 7d378de903c942e3ba31bdcd49a6b742
msgid "Miscellaneous: female to female 3 wire receiver / servo cables, a battery strap, tie wraps and some assorted hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:55
#: 520f03b9f77843daba34e3874ff2c2b3
msgid "You will also need an adjustable soldering iron, rosin cored solder, blue thread locker and some small Metric Allen wrenches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:62
#: ef04c9d66a6443d6a011bb6b48645c76
msgid "Frame and Motor Assembly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:64
#: 816b80065bcc45cbbfb8aad7da496c15
msgid "Get the \"manual\": `F330_User_Manual_v1.6_en.pdf <http://dl.djicdn.com/downloads/flamewheel/en/F330_User_Manual_v1.6_en.pdf>`__. (If there is a more recent version, you may find it in the `DJI website Flamewheel support section <https://www.dji.com/flame-wheel-arf/download>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:68
#: 96727f7757914cfbbc66318c672f4456
msgid "It is more of an assembly diagram than a manual, but the pictures are definitely useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:71
#: dc35a0f57a1b4248808d5720a842daf3
msgid "The DJI instructions show soldering the ESCs to the Power Distribution Board (bottom frame plate) first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:74
#: 3788516086f146578e775b0736ac5553
msgid "In our example they were put in after frame assembly because it makes it possible to fit things more closely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:76
#: a7af076088464b3a8e9deb10ef5d9604
msgid "But it does require a bit of creativity when soldering the ESC leads to the bottom plate / power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:78
#: 2517555d63f343939e22016ecc22d563
msgid "Your choice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:80
#: 825bb369c63a457fa76add895f789d48
msgid "Use Blue or purple removable thread locker very sparingly on the threads of the Allen screws when you assemble the frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:83
#: 3d0fc21c40704318b2e8d36bf7424745
msgid "Try to keep excess thread locker off of the plastic. This is not actually achievable, but do the best you can."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:86
#: 4ce6dcff1d1b4e66b506f621a7feaaea
msgid "Motor and frame screws have a shoulder on them and you need to tighten them all sufficiently so that the shoulder fully seats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:89
#: ce388614eb9e4123a92dead55c8a3ab3
msgid "A good method is to install all screws (with Locktite) loosely then tighten all the screws on each frame arm one at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:91
#: 37ba62c00850428a97c96bc10a880ee5
msgid "Do this in one sitting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:93
#: 8bec02a9498340808ca036444bcab6da
msgid "When installing the motors, pre-bend the motor leads upward where they exit the motor bottom so that the motor can sit flat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:96
#: 5aba8d23efb14d2e8287397ae12c3763
msgid "Have the leads exit towards the center of the copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:97
#: 149f1a16185643998b34f23503dcf91d
msgid "Motor bottom screws are off set and it can only be installed 2 ways, toward the center is correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:98
#: b51b3dcf6a1d49b0be2e1b2d3e3e291d
msgid "The motor screws are short and it is tricky to start the first screw on the motor bottom."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:99
#: d7f1402604a74ca2902fb91dfb2e3b68
msgid "Ensure that the motor leads are not pushing the motor up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:100
#: 1fb23996f1694ff0a69edbb550d2dcfc
msgid "Use blue Locktite on each screw and install all 4 screws for a motor loosely and then tighten them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:102
#: 126899313f41469fb1f55236abab3361
msgid "Thread the motor leads down through the first 2 large frame member holes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:104
#: 3a8302d628fc4334b3216ec0de0f10f2
msgid "Or you can run them around the frame member if you prefer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:109
#: 174519ec3b004e3f9322007da7640780
msgid "Be careful to wire motors to the PixHawk using the ArduPilot numbering convention for QuadX below. The numbering convention in the DJI FlameWheel F450 instructions are different, and incorrect writing leads to attitude instability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:117
#: 15a6be03d0684f3fa00b964d3538a441
msgid "ESC Installation and Soldering the Power Distribution Board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:119
#: 872a558258b34499ba46542e67569a75
msgid "Install the ESCs with tie wraps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:121
#: 6e4f62c40d644bf28f284e9c5877d347
msgid "Thread the Tie Wraps from front to back through the frame members and between the motor bullet connector sockets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:122
#: 3b6fe4b8177c4151a14875bf050cb907
msgid "Install the ESC power leads through the slot under the bottom of the frame member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:123
#: e10c91800b7d423dbc0228a6cebe8fc3
msgid "Then trim and solder them to the power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:124
#: 5d54f79dbbbe4708961c9372cbd21364
msgid "This is a little harder than going around the outside of the frame but is neater and provides a little more battery clearance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:126
#: 081f26ae2ae344759dbe3ff62a3ea210
msgid "The above illustration shows a power distribution \"Y\" connector which functions the same as the FlameWheel's built in power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:128
#: 4db194fb1a8b4475a3912cee6507c43d
msgid "When you solder the ESC and Battery power leads to the power distribution board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:130
#: a44bd18a124c4920afc0b9e33d4a7293
msgid "Flux and preheat both the pads and the wire in order to get a properly tinned (wet) solder joint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:131
#: 31058e48a5114420962731c39030eed0
msgid "The board can soak up quite a bit of heat so set your soldering iron sufficiently hot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:133
#: 041d9cf7c9a2469ebb8047cadea52be9
msgid "The DJI ARF FlameWheel kits have Opto ESCs which do not include a BEC so you will need an external power supply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:135
#: e5fc919e5b5944c893e8e21a5441da41
msgid "The APM, PX4 and Pixhawk are now available with a power supply you can use, other wise you will need to buy a BEC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:136
#: 3ca4373f9ae44548b335a1e0223b20be
msgid "Castle Creations makes an excellent and very reliable 10/5 amp BEC for about $20.00."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:137
#: 13eb1817f311462190015b04112474da
msgid "Use a switching BEC in any case, they are more reliable and a lot more efficient than linear ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:139
#: a4a5ac8211cc4367bbd677a9ca770ae8
msgid "You do not need to and in fact can't balance the DJI ESCs as shown elsewhere in the Copter Wiki."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:141
#: a7dfff734cad40c4a8e2def5937c4899
msgid "DJI ESCs are digital, optically isolated, are completely pre-balanced at the factory and work fine out of the box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:147
#: 6d7270cd590343ebb68550a233bece44
msgid "Reduced Vibration Installation of the Autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:149
#: 826314bdeca7446db5a1e7290a06c3fe
msgid "The autopilots require special attention be paid to removing as much vibration from the autopilot as possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:152
#: 8b55e62a60ec48dc988f16dff1e3f875
msgid "This F330 FlameWheel has a special anti-vibration suspension mounting of the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:154
#: af28670b843443df8a76dc66d601d4b9
msgid "It uses a folded over 1/16\" O-ring at each corner of the autopilot around a screw sticking out of a small standoff."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:155
#: c054f9042b3341e78a084eb146ce76f1
msgid "If you choose to use this method leave 1/10\" to 1/8\" clearance from each board corner for proper short coupled spacing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:157
#: 2f3b32d2fb384add8e7eec7f9bc4a05f
msgid "The F330 requires minor surgery with a Dremel tool on each frame arm to achieve proper hole spacing in the top plate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:160
#: 7fa926058da14397ac1d83e1edafd126
msgid "Kyosho Zeal Gel is an easy to install and fully satisfactory alternative to the O-ring suspension method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:163
#: c4daa03f2e0d4bb580c8f8971b1ae4c8
msgid "Simply put a 3/4 inch square of adhesive backed Kyosho Zeal Gel under each corner of the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:165
#: be5ade60a6cc4621ba9213a947e8fb41
msgid "And secure the autopilot with a Velcro strap over 1/2\" of soft foam in light tension. (Do NOT over tighten!)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:168
#: 75f0beed609e41c180ec62e1aa5fe2aa
msgid "Either the Kyosho Zeal Gel or the O-ring suspension method will allow you to limit vibration to about 1/10 G which is fine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:170
#: 29ca777d464846eca12de6062da5878a
msgid "Anti-vibration techniques, methods and \"tuning\" are covered in greater detail in the :ref:`Anti-Vibration section of the Wiki <common-vibration-damping>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:172
#: 44d723bc85604b5c902405f60eb15ab9
msgid "Compensation for compass interference from the motors is :ref:`covered here! <common-magnetic-interference>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:173
#: bf643725e8ba4b76909eac41f275cd54
msgid "Correct wiring of the autopilot and configuration for flight are covered extensively elsewhere in the Wiki."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:181
#: f6c2ec2f75de4561a51761e42f5f94b5
msgid "\\*The Velcro on the board and frame above is not in use and is not actually touching\\*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:185
#: 1c5121ef5605441483c7bbe8901f515f
msgid "Getting Ready to Fly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:187
#: 5eb0e818c77743e3ad8f14f47382336e
msgid "Our construction method allows the battery to be inserted between the two frame plates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:190
#: 1005da0b43cb4b59a2d0ab6b707b06b3
msgid "This is an optimal location regarding the QuadCopter's center of gravity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:192
#: 3b59925c24d24fbcbf02965fdf596219
msgid "The 2650mah LiPo Turnigy Nano battery used here is as large as will comfortably fit, but it will permit 15 minute plus flights."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:194
#: 4ee026331a6242b486fb6bb45ad172a0
msgid "Cover bottom frame power distribution solder joints with liquid electrical tape or silicone to prepare for the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:196
#: f5642d8ba2dc45a68b3bc6ccb55a59fb
msgid "Wrap the battery in bubble wrap and tape it in place to provide additional electrical isolation from the solder joints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:198
#: d1d9e96ac2c54d9f82f02923d210820b
msgid "This will also provide cushioning from vibration and sub-optimal \"landings\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:200
#: 7f1b13fc4eed48cd9ab83d669af5daff
msgid "Use a Velcro battery strap through the frames bottom slots to retain the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:203
#: 14e83b999bb24611bc25e034948259e4
msgid "The stock 8\" DJI props that are supplied with the F330 ARF kit work fine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:206
#: 042b6968325648bfb332b9be21b3233d
msgid "However the F330 FlameWheel can definitely benefit from a 9\" prop (10\" will not fit on the F330)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:208
#: ddcbc0cf044b4e0aa0a0c7c7359eb38c
msgid "GemFan 9\" multirotor \"Carbon Filled\" props are only $2.00 each and are superior to the stock 8\" props."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:210
#: f06b810415b84c19806135d7a6437615
msgid "These GemFans are almost impossible to break and the 9\" ones are considerably more efficient than the stock 8\" props."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:212
#: ad70cc83a436483b926520b472d62c2d
msgid "9\" GemFan propellers are not made to fit the oval hubs of the DJI Motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:214
#: 303f94adba0f4aabac23b1514f195525
msgid "But you can carefully bore them out to about .31\" with an ordinary drill and they will fit perfectly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:216
#: 911029fc47854bd6a9238d465bb5c976
msgid "On My F450 Flamewheel, I use 11\" GemFan propellers bored out the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:218
#: 4fd3ecb2c1e94ed3a0d62fa8f61328ff
msgid "Generally a larger prop diameter is better so long as you don't exceed motor or ESC maximums or cause over heating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:220
#: d359086b204741efae96023196f1cfef
msgid "Make sure the propellers are right side up (printing on top), this won't fly worth a damn if they are upside down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:223
#: 51ac84fd71c947728fc45fba8d813d1f
msgid "The ESCs and motors automatically disarm after 10 seconds without the motor turning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:226
#: 6cbbfb3c630c48ec95077ea7e91deb14
msgid "So anytime you have remained stationary (on the ground) for over 10 seconds you will need to rearm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:228
#: 541b7276c0ac4560ac215811d378896b
msgid "This is an excellent safety feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:230
#: 24a8b3e2f3a44d6f97a876544c1ac105
msgid "You will need to Install Mission Planner software on your PC as instructed elsewhere in this Wiki."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:233
#: 149d5912f99d4deba6e3d8ac8e2db4a8
msgid "You will then need to use Mission Planner to load the QuadCopter firmware to your autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:235
#: 2c7435e9693a442f9796bdf76ea8a61b
msgid "And you will then need to set up various flight parameters for your FlameWheel in the Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:237
#: 3f4a281fe2684414b8b3ef949c9c6719
msgid "(Do Not Attempt to Calibrate the DJI Opto ESCs and Do Not install the propellers until directed to do so)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:240
#: c2343fb5b3e74a1e8c9c6b396cc00fe1
msgid "To prepare to fly place your copter on your takeoff location, turn your transmitter on and plug in the copter's battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:243
#: 3c336ecd78964ba9b98012ed2ce510b7
msgid "(If you have a PX4 or Pixhawk autopilot depress the start button for five seconds)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:245
#: aec4bbceece44ff89a86da1022135191
msgid "The ESC's should emit a short series of musical notes and then be quiet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:247
#: 1de0cef02264471d9b6d885501aab4d7
msgid "You are then ready to arm by holding the throttle stick down and to the right for 5 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:249
#: b6711048d5264cb7a038b8bfd8f119e0
msgid "After arming you must throttle up the motors within 10 seconds or you will need to re-arm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:251
#: 2abb0113b5194d56b0bf385c3df07ca3
msgid "When you are done flying disarm by holding the throttle down and to the left for 5 seconds and disconnect the battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:253
#: ca815a3f8a284cc798eb5955ba9d812f
msgid "A good set of initial PIDs for flying the FlameWheel F330 or F450 in Stabilize Mode (as of Copter version 3.0.1) are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/dji-f330-flamewheel.rst:255
#: 16956b5cc9ae4d49bd62a1d4a957bf32
msgid "Rate (Roll & Pitch) P = .09 and I = .045 and Stabilize (Roll & Pitch) P = 4.0"
msgstr ""
